-- title:
--   Section of 𝒪(mε) non-vanishing at a maximal ideal
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a Noetherian commutative ring, let $c : C \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ be a proper morphism of schemes which is smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, and let $\varepsilon$ be a section of $c$ over the identity of $\operatorname{Spec} R$, i.e. a pair consisting of a morphism $\varepsilon_1 : \operatorname{Spec} R \to C$ together with a proof that $\varepsilon_1$ followed by $c$ is the identity. Let $\mathcal V$ be a two-affine open cover of $C$: two affine opens $U_0, U_1$ with $U_0 \sqcup U_1 = \top$ and $U_0 \sqcap U_1$ affine. Let $g$ be a natural number with the property that for every algebraically closed field $k$, every morphism $s : \operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec} R$, every field extension $L/k$, every `CurveModel` $M$ for $(k, L)$ (an integral scheme, proper and smooth of relative dimension $1$ over $k$, with prescribed identification of $L$ with its function field, a bijection between its closed points and the places of $L/k$ matching stalks with valuation subrings, and with finite sets contained in affine opens), every isomorphism $e : M.C \cong C \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R} \operatorname{Spec} k$ such that $e$ followed by the second projection is the structure morphism of $M$, every divisor $K_c$ on the places of $L/k$ and every natural number $g'$: if $\ell(D) - \ell(K_c - D) = \deg D + 1 - g'$ for all divisors $D$, where $\ell$ denotes the $k$-dimension of the Riemann–Roch space, then $g' = g$. Assume $2g \le m$ and $1 \le m$, and let $\mathfrak m$ be a point of $\operatorname{Spec} R$ whose prime ideal is maximal. Then there is a morphism of $\mathcal O_C$-modules $s$ from the unit object to $(\varepsilon_1^{\mathrm{ker}})^{m}$`.invModule`, the dual of the module of the $m$-th power of the ideal sheaf data of $\varepsilon_1$, such that the image of $\mathfrak m$ under $\varepsilon_1$ does not lie in the support of the zero-scheme ideal sheaf of $s$, the latter being the infimum of those ideal sheaf data $J$ with the ideal generated by the coefficients of $s$ on each affine open $U$ contained in $J$ at $U$.
--
--   This is the global existence, over a Noetherian base, of a section of $\mathcal O(m\varepsilon)$ on a smooth proper geometrically integral relative curve which does not vanish at the point $\varepsilon(\mathfrak m)$ of the fibre over a maximal ideal, for $m \ge \max(2g, 1)$ with $g$ the genus determined by Riemann–Roch on the geometric fibres; it combines the corresponding statement on the fibre with surjectivity of restriction of global sections (cohomology and base change in degree zero). It is used in the construction of sections with prescribed vanishing behaviour disjoint from $\varepsilon$, as needed for producing Weierstrass-type coordinates on the relative curve.
